      "gitCommit": {
        "shortHash": "d8894a4",
        "hash": "d8894a4ea7166b75cca3d3dd2b81e476aa512b88",
        "subject": "S6b fix 1: link the map stylesheets and align pin geometry",
        "body": "S6b fix 1: link the map stylesheets and align pin geometry\n\nApp.razor now links lib/maplibre-gl/maplibre-gl.css and css/realm-map.css (plain relative URLs, as the\nno-static-files guard requires for our own files) in the order MudBlazor -> maplibre-gl.css -> tokens.css\n-> app.css -> realm-map.css, so MapLibre's marker and attribution rules and our pin, chip and attribution\nrules actually apply.\n\n[X-01] now also asserts that the page links the four stylesheets in that order and that the browser applied\nmaplibre-gl.css and realm-map.css, so this cannot regress unnoticed again.\n\nNo change to realm-map.css or realmMap.js: checked against the real CSS and JS in Chromium at 412 x 915, the\ngeometry already matches 01 sections 4.2 to 4.4 once the sheets load (attribution 48 x 48 with a 12 px right\ngap, discs 48 / 44 px with a 4 px solid ring, chip centred on the pin and 8 px above it). AC-18's 0.14\nalpha for demo-offline and the ~10.85 zoom stay as D74 says.\n\nROOT CAUSE: App.razor never linked maplibre-gl.css or realm-map.css (and realmMap.js does not inject them),\nso .maplibregl-marker was not position:absolute (pins stacked in flow, invisible), the compact attribution\nsummary was a full-width block (412 px) and the pin, disc and chip rules were absent (disc 10.98 px, chip\ncentre 351.48).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KBQausaArk3u4LVWi4qxwu\n",
        "author": {
